{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/100926-the-hunt-is-on","id":100926,"title":"The Hunt Is On","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-28T16:01:20-07:00","id":100926,"title":"The Hunt Is On","content":"Werewolves hunt, right? Their defining feature is that they're not really fighters, but hunters.<br /> <br /> What sort of role do chase/hunt scenes (as opposed to fight scenes) have in your Werewolf: the Forsaken games? How much time of your average Werewolf game sessions is spent on the hunt, whether the PCs are predators or prey?<br /> <br /> I'd be very grateful, too, about interesting stories about werewolves and hunts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T17:25:42-07:00","id":100982,"title":"","content":"The first thing that pops into my mind is the investigative hunt. Something is happening, why? who or what is responsible? how do we deal with -that- afterwards. If it's a ridden or a sharta with human ties, it makes it difficult to simply &quot;disappear&quot; the person.<br /> <br /> A spirit which specifically targets children as hosts to be urged imply subjecting a child to what amounts to torture to rid it from the possessing spirit and... who would kill a kid?<br /> <br /> In the spirit wilds, when a pack is establishing dominance over what they will call territory, there's likely already the predators and spirits at the top of the food chain there. Do you dogpile one of these spirits and bind him as your totem? That's hunting in hostile territory, more than likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T06:15:43-07:00","id":101225,"title":"","content":"Assassination hunts. Your target isn't much of a warrior. He gets Down and Dirty rules... once you track him down after the chase scene. <br /> <br /> Truthfully, I don't spend a lot of time on combats. I spend a lot of time on prepping for combats","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-29T13:14:10-07:00","id":101451,"title":"","content":"The last two major battles I ran in my werewolf game primarily focused on the hunt side of it.<br /> <br /> In the first case, the pack was aware of a Beshilu presence in their town, and had that morning heard a hive call screech out, so they gathered for a hunt. They knew of three locations which might have rats, but no solid information, and so gathered up to track them through the Shadow. It was a good look at the spirit wilds; once they picked up the scent, they followed the rats' path through various locations and backtrails, found one of their main nests (then empty) and were forced to follow into the physical world. The combat was still rather nasty and took a while to get through, but the hunt took something like an hour and a half, trying to pick up what they'd been doing and where.<br /> <br /> In our latest sessions, the were hunting a cult of spirit sorcerers in a university. The shadow was more hostile here, and the cult had been doing some weird things which they paused to investigate, and their target was alerted that they were coming, so they had to briefly chase him through the basements, only to get a glimpse of him getting into a car. A brief chase scene followed, where the scout kept pace and the pack followed - until they crossed into someone else's territory. Finally, when they reached the lair, it was a slow cautious stalking through traps, ambushed, and trapped spirits.<br /> <br /> The pack I'm running for are high exp combat monsters, so I've been trying to involve more tactics and hunting to make it interesting, particularly since I've heard Idigam Chronicles will be more focused on hunting. Its worked out pretty well in these last few cases, I think, but its something I'm still refining.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 03-31-2014, 07:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}